<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minamoto no Yoritomo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1147–1199</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Yoritomo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minamoto no Yoritomo was the founder and first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> shogunate. Leading the Minamoto clan to victory over the Taira in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a> of 1180–1185, he set up a warrior government at Kamakura, appointed military governors and stewards across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and destroyed the Northern Fujiwara in 1189. He received the title of shogun in 1192.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo.jpg" alt="Minamoto no Yoritomo" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fujiwara no Takanobu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minamoto_no_Yoritomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
